Theorem DP-3: is_rc_inc_elidable truth table — Once AND Linear

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - is_rc_inc_elidable : AimsState -> Bool per Annex E §AIMS DP-3 +
      Appendix C truth table
    - CN-1 invariant (Annex E §AIMS CN-1): Consumption = Dead <=>
      Cardinality = Absent bidirectional; canonical states satisfy the
      bidirectional equivalence
    - DP-3 is a pure boolean predicate over Cardinality x Consumption;
      Access / Uniqueness / Locality / Shape / Effect are non-load-bearing
      for the DP-3 obligation

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState (canonical, post-CN-1).
      is_rc_inc_elidable(s)
        <=> (s.cardinality = Once AND s.consumption = Linear)

    DP-3 captures the move-once semantics: a value used exactly once
    (Cardinality = Once) and consumed linearly (Consumption = Linear) has
    its caller-side inc balanced by callee-side move (no RcInc needed).

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Enumerate the 4 Consumption x 3 Cardinality = 12 product states.
      (b) Apply CN-1 canonical filter; 7 canonical states remain (mirrors
          DP-2 filter structure).
      (c) For each canonical row, verify the predicate value equals the
          Appendix C row partition value.

    Part (a) — Appendix C row partition (3 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: Cardinality = Once, Consumption = Linear -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (both conjuncts hold); move-once.
      Row 2: Cardinality = Once, Consumption != Linear -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (second conjunct fails).
      Row 3: Cardinality != Once (Absent / Many), any Consumption -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (first conjunct fails).

    Part (b) — CN-1 canonical filter (identical to DP-2):
      Product cardinality: 4 x 3 = 12.
      Infeasible (eliminated by CN-1): 5 states.
      Canonical subset: 7 states.
        Canonical rows: (Dead, Absent),
                       (Linear, Once), (Linear, Many),
                       (Affine, Once), (Affine, Many),
                       (Unrestricted, Once), (Unrestricted, Many).

    Part (c) — soundness equality on canonical rows:
      Canonical row (Linear, Once) -> DP-3 = true (Appendix Row 1).
      Canonical rows (Affine, Once), (Unrestricted, Once) -> DP-3 = false
        (Appendix Row 2: Once + != Linear).
      Canonical rows (Dead, Absent), (Linear, Many), (Affine, Many),
        (Unrestricted, Many) -> DP-3 = false (Appendix Row 3: != Once).
      Negative-direction witness: DP-3 = true on EXACTLY the canonical
      (Once, Linear) row; the 6 other canonical rows return false. The
      tightness of the conjunction is observable.

    DP-3 vs former DP-10 distinction:
      DP-10 (REMOVED) claimed `O AND L AND 1 ==> RC = 1` unsound:
      backward analysis proves no future duplication but NOT no existing
      aliases. DP-3 is the SOUND inc-elision predicate: a value with
      Cardinality = Once + Consumption = Linear has no future duplication;
      the caller's RcInc is balanced by the callee's move at the single
      use site. Uniqueness != Unique is permitted by DP-3 (the existing
      alias from upstream RcInc is decoupled from the inc-elision
      decision — the existing alias has its own ref count entry and
      DP-3 only affects the duplicate inc that would otherwise be
      emitted at this use site).

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 12-product / 7-canonical enumeration per
        section_05::verify_dp3_rc_inc_elidable; the verifier applies the
        CN-1 canonical filter and checks the soundness equality on every
        canonical row + asserts exactly 1 canonical row yields true)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-3 via 12-product / 7-canonical-post-CN-1 enumeration per Annex E §AIMS DP-3 + Appendix C; exactly 1 canonical row (Once, Linear) satisfies the predicate
